---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ToolHero from '../../components/tools/ToolHero.astro';
import ToolHowItWorks from '../../components/tools/ToolHowItWorks.astro';
import ToolFAQ from '../../components/tools/ToolFAQ.astro';

const today = '2026-06-13T00:00:00+00:00';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is the Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator?',
    a: 'The Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator is a free browser-based tool that creates realistic-looking but completely non-functional API key placeholders for popular providers including OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Azure, and Stripe. Every key is generated locally inside your browser using the Web Crypto API, with no data sent to any server, and the generated keys cannot authenticate with any real API.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is the Mock API Key Generator free and safe to use?',
    a: 'Yes, the Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator is completely free with no usage limits and no signup required. It is safe because all generation happens client-side using <code>crypto.getRandomValues()</code> from the Web Crypto API. Your browser generates the random strings locally, and nothing is transmitted to a server, database, or third party. Disconnect from the internet after loading the page and the tool continues to work perfectly.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What API key formats does this generator support?',
    a: 'The Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator supports six provider formats. OpenAI uses the <code>sk-proj-</code> prefix followed by 48 characters. Anthropic uses <code>sk-ant-api03-</code> followed by approximately 95 alphanumeric characters. Google uses the <code>AIzaSy</code> prefix with 35 characters. Azure generates a 32-character hexadecimal string. Stripe uses <code>sk_test_</code> with 24 characters. The generic format produces a <code>mock_</code> prefix with 32 characters for any custom provider.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I generate a fake OpenAI API key for my tutorial or test environment?',
    a: 'Select the OpenAI checkbox in the Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator and click Generate. The tool produces a key in the current OpenAI format starting with <code>sk-proj-</code>, for example <code>sk-proj-xxxxxDEMOxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx</code>. The key looks realistic in screenshots and code snippets but contains the word DEMO so it is immediately identifiable as a placeholder. Copy it with one click and paste it into your tutorial, README, or <code>.env.example</code> file.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I safely commit a generated dummy API key to my GitHub repository?',
    a: 'Yes, because every key generated by the Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator contains a visible placeholder marker (DEMO, or a hex-safe marker like dead for hexadecimal formats such as Azure) and is mathematically incapable of authenticating with any real service. However, security tools like GitHub Secret Scanning and gitleaks may still flag realistic-looking strings. To avoid false positives, add an allowlist comment in your code such as <code>// gitleaks:allow</code> or use a <code>.gitleaks.toml</code> exclude pattern for DEMO substrings. Always review your secret scanner documentation for the exact syntax.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does a real Anthropic Claude API key look like, and how does your generator match it?',
    a: 'A real Anthropic API key starts with <code>sk-ant-api03-</code> followed by approximately 95 alphanumeric characters, as confirmed by Anthropic\'s official documentation and SDK source code. The Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator creates keys with the exact same prefix and length, embedding DEMO in the character string so it is visually obvious as a placeholder while maintaining the correct format for UI mockups, Storybook components, and documentation screenshots.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do developers use mock API keys in CI/CD pipelines and GitHub Actions?',
    a: 'Developers set generated mock keys as environment variables in GitHub Actions workflow files, Docker Compose configurations, and Jenkins pipelines to test application startup and validation logic without exposing real credentials. For example, setting <code>OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-xxxxxDEMOxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx</code> in a public CI workflow lets your app boot and run unit tests that do not require live API calls. The Best Answer Hub generator produces copy-paste-ready <code>.env.example</code> blocks for exactly this purpose.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why does my app silently fail when I use a hand-rolled placeholder like sk-placeholder?',
    a: 'Many SDKs and frameworks validate the format of an API key before making a network request. A placeholder like <code>sk-placeholder</code> often fails prefix validation or length checks, causing the SDK to reject it silently without a clear error message. The Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator produces keys that match the exact regex patterns and character lengths expected by official SDKs from OpenAI, Anthropic, and Google, so your application initializes correctly and fails only at the authentication stage with a clear 401 error.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I generate multiple mock API keys at once for different providers?',
    a: 'Yes. The Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator supports bulk generation: select any combination of OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Azure, Stripe, and Generic, then click Generate All. The tool instantly creates realistic placeholders for every selected provider and formats them as a ready-to-paste <code>.env.example</code> block. This is ideal for multi-provider tutorials, microservice demos, and testing environment setups that require several keys at once.',
  },
  {
    q: "What's the difference between a mock API key, a test API key, and a dummy API key?",
    a: 'The terms are often used interchangeably, but there are subtle differences. A test API key is usually issued by the provider itself, for example Stripe provides <code>sk_test_</code> keys that hit a sandbox environment and are functional. A dummy API key is typically a hardcoded string like <code>YOUR_KEY_HERE</code> with no realistic format. A mock API key from the Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator sits in between: it has the exact format and length of a real key but is mathematically non-functional, making it perfect for screenshots, documentation, and UI testing where visual authenticity matters.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I create a realistic-looking .env.example file with fake keys for my project?',
    a: 'Select the providers your project uses in the Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator, click Generate, then copy the <code>.env.example</code> block. The output includes commented labels and realistic-looking placeholders such as <code>OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-xxxxxDEMOxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx</code> and <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-api03-xxxxxDEMOxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx</code>. Paste this directly into your repository as <code>.env.example</code> so new contributors see exactly which environment variables are required without any real credentials being exposed.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will secret scanners like GitHub Secret Scanning or gitleaks flag these generated fake keys?',
    a: 'Possibly. Tools like GitHub Secret Scanning, gitleaks, and TruffleHog use regex patterns to detect key formats, and they cannot distinguish a realistic-looking fake from a real key without additional context. The Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator embeds a visible placeholder marker (DEMO, or a hex-safe equivalent for hexadecimal key formats) in every key to help human reviewers identify them, but automated scanners may still flag them. To prevent alert fatigue, add explicit allowlist rules in <code>.gitleaks.toml</code> or comments like <code>// gitleaks:allow</code> next to any committed placeholder keys.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What regex pattern should I use to validate an OpenAI API key format in my code?',
    a: 'For basic prefix validation of modern OpenAI project keys, use the pattern <code>^sk-proj-[A-Za-z0-9]{40,}$</code>. For legacy user keys, use <code>^sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}$</code>. The Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator displays the matching regex for each provider alongside the generated key. For Anthropic keys, use <code>^sk-ant-api03-[A-Za-z0-9]{90,}$</code>. For Google, use <code>^AIzaSy[A-Za-z0-9_-]{35}$</code>. These patterns catch typos and copy-paste errors before your application wastes time on a failed authentication request.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I use a mock API key for local development with Ollama, LiteLLM, or other local AI servers?',
    a: 'Yes. Local AI gateways like LiteLLM and Ollama often require an API key in the request header even when the model runs entirely on your machine. The Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator produces format-correct placeholders that satisfy these validation checks. For example, setting <code>OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-xxxxxDEMOxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx</code> in your <code>.env</code> file lets LiteLLM route requests to a local model without ever touching OpenAI\'s servers. The key passes format validation but will fail if accidentally sent to a real provider endpoint.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is it legal to use a realistic-looking fake API key in enterprise documentation or training materials?',
    a: 'In most jurisdictions, using a clearly labeled non-functional placeholder for educational or documentation purposes is legal and standard practice. However, some enterprises have internal security policies that prohibit realistic-looking fake credentials in training materials to prevent social engineering or confusion. The Best Answer Hub Mock API Key Generator embeds DEMO markers in every key to make the non-functional status unmistakable. If your organization has strict data-handling policies, consult your security team before using format-accurate placeholders in official documentation.',
  },
];

const steps = [
  { title: 'Select providers', description: 'Choose one or more API key formats: OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Azure, Stripe, or Generic. Click Generate All to create placeholders for every selected provider instantly.' },
  { title: 'Copy your keys', description: 'Each generated key matches the exact prefix, length, and character set of a real provider key. Click Copy on any card to grab a single key, or copy the entire .env.example block in one click.' },
  { title: 'Paste with confidence', description: 'Use the keys in tutorials, Storybook components, CI/CD configs, .env.example files, or local development. Every key contains a DEMO marker so it is visibly a placeholder.' },
];

const seo = {
  title: 'Mock API Key Generator — OpenAI, Claude, Google (2026)',
  description: 'Generate realistic non-functional API key placeholders for OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Azure, and Stripe. 100% client-side. No data sent to servers.',
  url: '/developer-toolbox/mock-api-key-generator/',
  type: 'WebPage' as const,
  datePublished: today,
  dateModified: today,
  breadcrumbs: [
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Developer Toolbox', url: '/developer-toolbox/' },
    { name: 'Mock API Key Generator', url: '/developer-toolbox/mock-api-key-generator/' },
  ],
  faq: faqs.map(f => ({ question: f.q, answer: f.a.replace(/<[^>]*>/g, '').replace(/\s{2,}/g, ' ').trim() })),
};
---

<BaseLayout seo={seo}>
  <ToolHero
    badge="Free Tool · No Data Sent to Servers"
    title="Mock API Key Generator:"
    accentText="Realistic placeholders for 6 providers"
    description="Generate non-functional but format-accurate API key placeholders for OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Azure, Stripe, and generic providers. Perfect for tutorials, CI/CD, .env.example files, and UI mockups. All generation runs in your browser via the Web Crypto API."
    backLink="/developer-toolbox/"
    backLabel="← Developer Toolbox"
  />

  <!-- Mock API Key Generator Interface -->
  <section class="py-6 md:py-8" aria-label="Mock API key generator">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-bae-ink mb-4">Mock API Key Generator</h2>

        <!-- Provider Selection -->
        <div class="mb-5">
          <p class="text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-2.5">Select providers to generate</p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2" id="provider-toggles">
            <label class="provider-label cursor-pointer inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-bae-ink hover:border-bae-primary transition-colors select-none">
              <input type="checkbox" class="provider-check accent-bae-primary" data-provider="openai" checked />
              OpenAI
            </label>
            <label class="provider-label cursor-pointer inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-bae-ink hover:border-bae-primary transition-colors select-none">
              <input type="checkbox" class="provider-check accent-bae-primary" data-provider="anthropic" checked />
              Anthropic
            </label>
            <label class="provider-label cursor-pointer inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-bae-ink hover:border-bae-primary transition-colors select-none">
              <input type="checkbox" class="provider-check accent-bae-primary" data-provider="google" checked />
              Google
            </label>
            <label class="provider-label cursor-pointer inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-bae-ink hover:border-bae-primary transition-colors select-none">
              <input type="checkbox" class="provider-check accent-bae-primary" data-provider="azure" checked />
              Azure
            </label>
            <label class="provider-label cursor-pointer inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-bae-ink hover:border-bae-primary transition-colors select-none">
              <input type="checkbox" class="provider-check accent-bae-primary" data-provider="stripe" checked />
              Stripe
            </label>
            <label class="provider-label cursor-pointer inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-bae-ink hover:border-bae-primary transition-colors select-none">
              <input type="checkbox" class="provider-check accent-bae-primary" data-provider="generic" />
              Generic
            </label>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Generate Button -->
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5">
          <button
            type="button"
            id="generate-btn"
            class="bg-bae-primary text-white text-sm font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded-bae-sm hover:bg-bae-accent transition-colors"
          >
            Generate All
          </button>
          <button
            type="button"
            id="clear-btn"
            class="bg-bae-bg text-bae-muted border border-bae-border text-sm font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded-bae-sm hover:border-bae-primary transition-colors"
          >
            Clear All
          </button>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-bae-muted">Keys contain a DEMO marker and cannot authenticate with any real API.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Generated Keys Output -->
        <div id="keys-output" class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-5"></div>

        <!-- .env.example Block -->
        <div class="bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm p-4">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-bold text-bae-ink">.env.example</h3>
            <button
              type="button"
              id="copy-env-btn"
              class="bg-bae-ink text-white text-[11px] font-semibold px-3 py-1.5 rounded-bae-sm hover:bg-bae-primary transition-colors"
            >
              Copy .env
            </button>
          </div>
          <textarea
            id="env-output"
            readonly
            class="w-full h-32 bg-white/50 border border-bae-border/50 rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 text-xs text-bae-ink font-mono resize-none focus:outline-none"
          ></textarea>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ToolHowItWorks steps={steps} />

  <!-- Scenario Section -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-8">What developers build with it</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-6">
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-bae-primary">Technical Writer, Documentation Team</span>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-bae-ink mt-2 mb-1">Screenshot-ready API documentation</h3>
          <p class="text-xs font-medium text-bae-primary mb-3">Professional docs without credential leaks</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Generate realistic OpenAI and Anthropic keys for API documentation, README files, and Medium tutorials. Readers see authentic-looking code blocks without any risk of leaked credentials.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-6">
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-bae-primary">Frontend Developer, Component Library</span>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-bae-ink mt-2 mb-1">Realistic form inputs for Storybook</h3>
          <p class="text-xs font-medium text-bae-primary mb-3">Realistic form inputs in 10 seconds</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Populate API key input fields in React, Vue, or Angular Storybook components with format-correct placeholders. The <code>sk-proj-</code> and <code>AIzaSy</code> prefixes make your UI look production-ready during design reviews.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-6">
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-bae-primary">DevOps Engineer, CI/CD Pipeline</span>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-bae-ink mt-2 mb-1">Safe public CI without secret exposure</h3>
          <p class="text-xs font-medium text-bae-primary mb-3">Test app boot in GitHub Actions</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Inject mock keys into public GitHub Actions workflows and Docker Compose files. Your application boots, validates environment variables, and runs unit tests without requiring real API credentials in repository secrets.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-6">
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-bae-primary">Backend Developer, API Gateway</span>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-bae-ink mt-2 mb-1">Test regex validation middleware</h3>
          <p class="text-xs font-medium text-bae-primary mb-3">Validate prefix checks before production</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Pass generated keys through your authentication middleware to verify prefix checks and length validation. Confirm that <code>sk-ant-api03-</code> keys trigger the Anthropic route and <code>AIzaSy</code> keys trigger the Google route before deploying.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mt-4">Scenarios are illustrative examples based on common use cases. Generated keys are non-functional placeholders and cannot authenticate with any real API.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ToolFAQ faqs={faqs} />

  <!-- Related Developer Tools CTA -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="bg-bae-primary-soft border border-bae-primary/15 rounded-bae p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-start md:items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-1">Explore more developer tools</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted">Also try <a href="/tools/json-formatter/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">JSON</a>, <a href="/tools/base64-encoder/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">Base64</a>, <a href="/tools/jwt-decoder/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">JWT</a>, <a href="/tools/regex-tester/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">Regex</a>, <a href="/tools/hash-generator/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">Hash</a>, <a href="/tools/url-encoder/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">URL</a>, and <a href="/tools/timestamp-converter/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">Timestamp</a>, all free, no signup.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/developer-toolbox/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-bae-ink text-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-bae-sm font-semibold text-sm no-underline hover:bg-bae-primary transition-colors shrink-0">
          Browse developer toolbox →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script is:inline>
    (function() {
      function copyText(text) {
        if (!text) return;
        if (navigator.clipboard && navigator.clipboard.writeText) {
          navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).catch(() => {});
        } else {
          const ta = document.createElement('textarea');
          ta.value = text;
          ta.style.position = 'fixed';
          ta.style.opacity = '0';
          document.body.appendChild(ta);
          ta.select();
          document.execCommand('copy');
          document.body.removeChild(ta);
        }
      }

      function generateRandomString(length, charset) {
        const array = new Uint8Array(length);
        crypto.getRandomValues(array);
        let result = '';
        for (let i = 0; i < length; i++) {
          result += charset[array[i] % charset.length];
        }
        return result;
      }

      function insertDemo(randomPart, charset) {
        // Use the uppercase DEMO marker when the charset can represent it; otherwise
        // fall back to a charset-safe marker (e.g. 'dead' for hex-only keys like Azure)
        // so the key stays visibly fake AND still matches its declared format regex.
        let demo = 'DEMO';
        if (charset && !demo.split('').every(function(c) { return charset.indexOf(c) !== -1; })) {
          demo = 'dead';
        }
        const insertPos = Math.floor(randomPart.length / 3);
        return randomPart.slice(0, insertPos) + demo + randomPart.slice(insertPos + demo.length);
      }

      const providers = {
        openai: {
          name: 'OpenAI',
          prefix: 'sk-proj-',
          length: 48,
          charset: 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789',
          regex: '^sk-proj-[A-Za-z0-9]{48,}$',
          envVar: 'OPENAI_API_KEY'
        },
        anthropic: {
          name: 'Anthropic',
          prefix: 'sk-ant-api03-',
          length: 95,
          charset: 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789',
          regex: '^sk-ant-api03-[A-Za-z0-9]{95,}$',
          envVar: 'ANTHROPIC_API_KEY'
        },
        google: {
          name: 'Google',
          prefix: 'AIzaSy',
          length: 35,
          charset: 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789_-',
          regex: '^AIzaSy[A-Za-z0-9_-]{35}$',
          envVar: 'GOOGLE_API_KEY'
        },
        azure: {
          name: 'Azure OpenAI',
          prefix: '',
          length: 32,
          charset: '0123456789abcdef',
          regex: '^[a-f0-9]{32}$',
          envVar: 'AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY'
        },
        stripe: {
          name: 'Stripe',
          prefix: 'sk_test_',
          length: 24,
          charset: 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789',
          regex: '^sk_test_[A-Za-z0-9]{24}$',
          envVar: 'STRIPE_API_KEY'
        },
        generic: {
          name: 'Generic',
          prefix: 'mock_',
          length: 32,
          charset: 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789',
          regex: '^mock_[A-Za-z0-9]{32}$',
          envVar: 'API_KEY'
        }
      };

      function generateKey(providerKey) {
        const p = providers[providerKey];
        const randomPart = generateRandomString(p.length, p.charset);
        const finalRandom = insertDemo(randomPart, p.charset);
        return p.prefix + finalRandom;
      }

      function generateAll() {
        const selected = [];
        document.querySelectorAll('.provider-check:checked').forEach(function(cb) {
          selected.push(cb.dataset.provider);
        });

        if (selected.length === 0) {
          document.getElementById('keys-output').innerHTML = '<p class="text-sm text-bae-muted col-span-full">Select at least one provider to generate keys.</p>';
          document.getElementById('env-output').value = '';
          return;
        }

        const outputContainer = document.getElementById('keys-output');
        outputContainer.innerHTML = '';
        const envLines = [];

        selected.forEach(function(pk) {
          const p = providers[pk];
          const key = generateKey(pk);

          const card = document.createElement('div');
          card.className = 'bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm p-4';
          card.innerHTML = '<div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">' +
            '<span class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-primary uppercase tracking-wider">' + p.name + '</span>' +
            '<button type="button" class="copy-key-btn bg-bae-ink text-white text-[11px] font-semibold px-2.5 py-1 rounded-bae-sm hover:bg-bae-primary transition-colors" data-key="' + key + '">Copy</button>' +
            '</div>' +
            '<code class="block text-xs text-bae-ink font-mono break-all bg-white/50 rounded-bae-sm px-2.5 py-2 border border-bae-border/50">' + key + '</code>' +
            '<p class="text-[10px] text-bae-muted mt-1.5">Regex: <code class="text-bae-primary">' + p.regex + '</code></p>';
          outputContainer.appendChild(card);

          envLines.push(p.envVar + '=' + key);
        });

        document.getElementById('env-output').value = '# Mock API Keys: Non-functional placeholders generated by Best Answer Hub\n' + envLines.join('\n');

        document.querySelectorAll('.copy-key-btn').forEach(function(btn) {
          btn.addEventListener('click', function() {
            copyText(this.dataset.key);
            this.textContent = 'Copied';
            setTimeout(function() { btn.textContent = 'Copy'; }, 1500);
          });
        });
      }

      document.getElementById('generate-btn').addEventListener('click', generateAll);
      document.getElementById('clear-btn').addEventListener('click', function() {
        document.querySelectorAll('.provider-check').forEach(function(cb) { cb.checked = false; });
        document.getElementById('keys-output').innerHTML = '';
        document.getElementById('env-output').value = '';
      });
      document.getElementById('copy-env-btn').addEventListener('click', function() {
        const envText = document.getElementById('env-output').value;
        copyText(envText);
        this.textContent = 'Copied';
        setTimeout(function() { this.textContent = 'Copy .env'; }.bind(this), 1500);
      });

      // Generate on load with defaults
      generateAll();
    })();
  </script>
